  "task": {
    "objective": "Physically carry both evacuees from the east rooms to the shelter at (1,3) before all rescuers are disabled or tick 128.",
    "natural_termination": "Both evacuees rescued, or every rescuer has zero health; natural completion has priority over timeout on the same tick.",
    "interaction": "Lantern and beacon illumination changes other roles visibility and the cells a loaded carrier can enter. Shared battery stock, exclusive bulky carrying, object competition, relay timing and moving dark hazards create action-dependent coordination.",
    "observation_access": "Each role sees its own status and public time/rescue totals. Current cell visibility uses a 17-sample rounded cell ray and Manhattan distance: radius one regardless of light, or radius four in illuminated cells. Shadows additionally require illumination. No other map cells, shadow phase, distant inventories or unseen object positions enter the role observation. Renderer uses the same visibility arrays.",
    "transition_order": "Movement uses pre-step illumination; rotating object interactions follow; charge/relay timers tick; shadows move every third tick; new light determines damage; rescue and terminal state are then evaluated."
  },
  "invariant_notes": [
    "Agent positions remain on non-wall cells; co-location is intentional.",
    "At most one lantern or evacuee is held per rescuer; role capabilities restrict lifting.",
    "Lantern charge is between 0 and 64, beacon ttl between 0 and 12, depot stock between 0 and 16, health between 0 and 3.",
    "Evacuee rescue is irreversible and counted once; lighting is recomputed from actual positions, switches, fuel and rays.",
    "Moving shadow phase is private except for consequences revealed through legal observations.",
